  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Between Saint-Tropez's two wildest beaches, this short stretch of coastal path skirts the rocky La Moutte headland, with views across the Gulf of Saint-Tropez to Sainte-Maxime opposite. Like the rest of the Var coastline, this path follows the route of the old "sentier des Douaniers", once walked by the customs officers who watched the coast for night-time smuggling.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs on a leash are accepted on this stretch between <a href="/en/fiche-plage-moutte-saint-tropez">La Moutte beach</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-salins-saint-tropez">Les Salins beach</a>: municipal order no. 1828/2026 (6 July 2026) expressly exempts walkers accompanied by dogs on a leash on the coastal path from its scope. On the beaches themselves, the same order allows dogs only from 6am to 9:30am and from 6:30pm to 10pm, from 16 July to 15 September 2026, and bans them outside those slots; the tourist office listing, for its part, states "dogs banned" on the La Moutte and Les Salins beaches, so check on site before setting paws on the sand.</p>
      <p>The same order (article 3) sets the conditions for moving about: the dog remains under its owner's constant responsibility, kept on a leash when other users approach and whenever circumstances require. Article 4 requires you to pick up waste immediately, not to disturb public tranquillity, not to damage natural areas and to respect fauna and flora. Dogs likely to be dangerous or in a regulated category must comply with the legislation in force.</p>
      <p>The order was signed on 6 July 2026, received by the prefecture and published on 21 July 2026; its slots cover the period from 16 July to 15 September 2026. It says nothing about the regime applying outside these dates: for the following season, re-read the order in force on the town's website before putting your dog on the sand.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: shade is rare on this exposed stretch, bring water for your dog, especially in high season, and keep the leash short when you meet other walkers.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>On the La Moutte side, Chemin des Treilles de la Moutte connects to Route des Salins. On the Salins side, a free municipal shuttle serves Place des Lices in summer. The neighbouring beach listings detail the rule specific to each: <a href="/en/fiche-plage-moutte-saint-tropez">La Moutte</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-salins-saint-tropez">Les Salins</a>.</p>
    </div>

